---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import PresentValueCalculator from '@/components/tools/calc/PresentValueCalculator.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="present-value-calculator">
  <PresentValueCalculator client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How the present value calculator works</h2>
    <p>
      The present value calculator finds what a future amount is worth today. Money you get later is worth
      less than the same money now, because money you have now can earn interest in the meantime. The
      calculator divides the future amount by the growth it would have at your rate.
    </p>
    <p>
      The formula is <code>PV = FV ÷ (1 + i)^n</code>. <code>FV</code> is the future amount,
      <code>i</code> is the rate per period and <code>n</code> is the number of periods. With yearly
      compounding, <code>i</code> is the annual rate and <code>n</code> is the number of years. With
      <code>m</code> compounding periods a year and <code>p</code> payments a year, the rate per payment
      period is <code>i = (1 + r ÷ m)^(m ÷ p) − 1</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Level payments add <code>PMT × (1 − (1 + i)^−n) ÷ i</code>. When the payments come at the start of
      each period, this is multiplied by <code>(1 + i)</code>. The discount factor
      <code>1 ÷ (1 + i)^n</code> is the value today of 1 received after <code>n</code> periods.
    </p>
    <h2>Worked example</h2>
    <p>
      10,000 received in 10 years, at 5% a year compounded yearly, has a present value of 6,139.13. The
      discount factor is 0.613913 and the discount is 3,860.87. With monthly compounding the present value
      falls to 6,071.61, because the effective annual rate is 5.116%.
    </p>
    <p>
      Add a payment of 500 at the end of each year for the same 10 years. The payments are worth 3,860.87
      today, so the total present value is 10,000.00. This is a bond with a 5% coupon priced at a 5% yield.
    </p>
    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>
      The rate is the same in every period. Years are rounded to whole payment periods. Tax, fees and
      inflation are not included. To see the value in today's prices, enter a rate after inflation.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
